# Fixed defect 135's P8, 2026-10-02 (lane recovery-b7; the certain-fix
# audit's `findings/P8-arrow_habit/`), a result written after `:` or `=>`
# with no body below the head. Symptom: `function stub(): pass` took the
# certain `-> pass` and `function answer(value: i64) => value` the certain
# `-> value`, and both stayed refused after `--apply`, `missing_body`, the
# word after the `:` or the `=>` being the body written on the head's line,
# Python's `pass` and an expression body. Cause: the result reading was
# taken as the one reading wherever what follows parses as a type, and a
# name does. It is `certain` now only where it is the line's one reading:
# over a body below the head, indented, tabbed or in braces, or in an
# `extern` group, where no signature has a body; over none it is a `guess`,
# and the message says where the body goes (`selfhost/parse/signature.hero`,
# `arrow_habit`). The missing body is told as before. Beside it: a stub
# whose word is a type, `(): i64` over nothing, is a guess too, the body
# being missing either way.

function stub(): pass  #~ expected_end_of_line

function answer(value: i64) => value  #~ missing_body expected_end_of_line

function sized(): i64  #~ missing_body expected_end_of_line

function with_a_body(): i64  #~ missing_body expected_end_of_line
    return 1

extern "stdlib.h"
    function abs(n: i32): i32  #~ expected_end_of_line

function main()
    print(abs(n: -1) + with_a_body())
